{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795290629,"nonce":"l0kzVCK3vXMyJF+QS/oOuB4VhHA=","message":"aba9e32 adds a flash log that makes this easier: info and above go to the evlog partition as well as USB, independent of the terminal, and survive a replug. After the lost-link test, run `fw-log` and compare it with the monitor output. Each line carries the time since boot. If the flash log has the lines the monitor lacks, it's a display problem; if both have the gap, it's a stall. The 10 s scan summary is USB-only now, so look for central's \"disconnecting\" line rather than the summaries.","files":null}]}